  "finding": "Edition 156 reconstructs exactly the same evidence while converting each original frame to packed RGB once. The exposed camera trace remains 34/42 correct observations, 8 withheld, 0 wrong overlaps and 0/30 hidden outputs, identical to 155. All eight app comparisons reproduce exact reference evidence. 7/7 harder generated cases meet their separate behavioral targets. Complete paired costs include the original verification. Defaults remain unchanged. On two alternating exposed-camera pairs, complete forced verification measured 180.85 seconds with original pixel access and 163.00 seconds with packed access (9.9% less time).",
  "validation": "55 selected Java checks and 164 desktop checks passed, with no failures or skipped cases. Seven new generated app comparisons and one exposed-camera comparison passed visible-control, forced-replay, cold-restart and source-integrity checks. Complete reference/packed-pixel evidence matches exactly. Independent geometry and exact-evidence gates passed; harder behavioral targets and measured cost benefit are reported separately. These are scoped checks, not a rerun of every historical capability. Recorded tests only."
